<title>LEBANON: Lebanon schoolteachers on one-day strike.</title>
<headline>Lebanon schoolteachers on one-day strike.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most of Lebanon's 70,000 schoolteachers went on a one-day strike on Wednesday over pay.</p>
<p>&quot;The strike is a success,&quot; teacher's union spokesman Hanna Gharib told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said under a new pay scale adopted by the government last July, retirement pensions were cut by 20 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;In addition we are not getting any social pay benefits. This is unacceptable. Today is just a warning strike to urge the government to abandon its policies,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Wednesday's strike left about one million students at Lebanon's public and private schools without teachers.</p>
</text>
